==English==

===Etymology===
Partly from {{inh|en|enm|discleymer}}, from {{der|en|xno|desclamer}}; and partly from {{af|en|disclaim|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪsˈkleɪm.ɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɪsˈkleɪm.ə/|a=RP}}
* {{hyph|en|dis|claim|er}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-disclaimer.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪmə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# One who disclaims, disowns, or renounces.
# A public [[disavowal]], as of responsibility, pretensions, claims, opinions, etc.
# {{lb|en|legal}} A denial, disavowal, or renunciation, as of a title, claim, interest, estate, or trust; relinquishment or waiver of an interest or estate.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1963|author=Parliament of the United Kingdom|title=w:Peerage Act 1963|chapter=section 1(1)|url=[s:Peerage Act 1963{{!}}Wikisource]|page=1|text=Subject to the provisions of this section, any person who, after the commencement of this Act, succeeds to a peerage in the peerage of England, Scotland, Great Britain or the United Kingdom may, by an instrument of '''disclaimer''' delivered to the Lord Chancellor within the period prescribed by this Act, disclaim that peerage for his life.}}
# {{lb|en|proscribed}} A [[disclosure]] of an interest, relationship, or the like.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=May 10 2012|author=Anant Rangaswami|title=No need for regulation in media – it’s happening by itself|journal=Firstpost|text=It interviewed, among others, the director of Vasant Valley School, owned by the same family that part-owns ''Mail Today''. No '''disclaimer''' was carried stating as much.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=April 23 2018|author=Hallie Detrick|title=What We Know About Sean Hannity's Shell Companies and Why It Matters|journal=Fortune|text=Though the fact that the two men do business together was disclosed on air, a recent op-ed penned by Lako and published on the Hannity show’s website had no such '''disclaimer'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* The use in the sense of a disclosure rather than a disavowal is a recent extension in meaning that may be considered incorrect usage.

